/// PersistentTerm — a node-global, build-once store for values that are
/// expensive to compute and read many times.
///
/// A class-side facade over Erlang's `persistent_term`, beside
/// `ProcessDictionary`. It is named for the mechanism because the mechanism's
/// cost model is what a user must know. Nothing here is per class or per
/// process; every key is shared by the whole node.
///
/// ```beamtalk
/// Object subclass: HpackHuffman
///   class tables -> Tuple =>
///     PersistentTerm at: #hpack_huffman_tables ifAbsentPut: [self buildTables]
/// ```
///
/// There is no `at:put:`. Replacing a value is the expensive operation, so a
/// caller who must replace one erases it first and sees the cost in the code.
///
/// ## Rules
/// - **Build-once only.** A read copies nothing, but `erase:` (and replacing a
///   value) makes the VM scan every process heap: a global GC, 0.1-0.3 ms,
///   and OTP has no batch erase. Do not call `erase:` on a hot path. For a
///   value that changes, use an Actor or `Ets`.
/// - **The block must be pure and deterministic.** Two processes that miss at
///   the same moment both run it. The helper reads again before storing and
///   keeps the first value, but a small window remains. A block that spawns
///   an actor or opens a resource would do so twice.
/// - **A raising block stores nothing.** The exception reaches the caller and
///   the next call runs the block again. A stored `nil` counts as present.
/// - **Do not store a pid, port, actor, class, `Ets` handle or block.** A
///   process identity outlives its process. On a miss, a value that is itself
///   a pid, an actor or a class is refused with a `type_error` naming the key;
///   store a registered name and look the process up. A process identity
///   nested inside a larger value is not detected. A stored block fails once
///   its module's code has been reloaded twice and purged.
/// - **Keys are node-global.** Use a package-prefixed Symbol, such as
///   `#mypkg_tables`. Internally the key is stored under
///   `{beamtalk_persistent_term, Key}`, so it cannot collide with the
///   runtime's own `persistent_term` keys.
/// - **Nothing is cleared on reload.** A value stays until `erase:` or until
///   the node stops. When the built value's shape changes, change the key
///   (`#mypkg_tables_v2`); in the REPL, `PersistentTerm erase:` rebuilds it
///   on the next read.
///
/// ## Deliberate exception to principles §4
/// After the builder method is edited at the REPL the stored value is stale,
/// while `beamtalk run` builds it fresh, so the value can differ between
/// surfaces until the key is changed or erased.
///
/// ## Examples
/// ```beamtalk
/// PersistentTerm at: #demo_squares ifAbsentPut: [(1 to: 5) collect: [:n | n * n]]
/// PersistentTerm at: #demo_squares ifAbsentPut: [Error signal: "not run"]
/// PersistentTerm erase: #demo_squares   // => true
/// ```
sealed typed Object subclass: PersistentTerm

  /// Answer the value stored under `key`. On a miss, evaluate `block`, store
  /// the result and answer it. The block is not run on a hit.
  ///
  /// If the block raises, nothing is stored. If another process stored first,
  /// that first value is kept and answered. A miss whose value is a pid, an
  /// actor or a class raises a `type_error`.
  ///
  /// ## Examples
  /// ```beamtalk
  /// PersistentTerm at: #doc_once ifAbsentPut: [42]   // => 42
  /// PersistentTerm at: #doc_once ifAbsentPut: [99]   // => 42
  /// ```
  class at: key :: Object ifAbsentPut: block :: Block(T) -> T =>
    (Erlang beamtalk_persistent_term) getOrPut: key block: block

  /// Answer the value stored under `key`, or the result of evaluating
  /// `block` if there is none. Stores nothing.
  ///
  /// ## Examples
  /// ```beamtalk
  /// PersistentTerm at: #doc_nothing_here ifAbsent: [0]   // => 0
  /// ```
  class at: key :: Object ifAbsent: block :: Block(T) -> Object | T =>
    (Erlang beamtalk_persistent_term) getOrElse: key block: block

  /// Answer whether a value is stored under `key`. A stored `nil` counts.
  ///
  /// ## Examples
  /// ```beamtalk
  /// PersistentTerm includesKey: #doc_nothing_here   // => false
  /// ```
  class includesKey: key :: Object -> Boolean =>
    (Erlang beamtalk_persistent_term) includesKey: key

  /// Remove the value stored under `key`. Answers `true` if a value was
  /// removed, `false` if there was none. **Forces a global GC**: do not call
  /// it on a hot path.
  ///
  /// ## Examples
  /// ```beamtalk
  /// PersistentTerm erase: #doc_nothing_here   // => false
  /// ```
  class erase: key :: Object -> Boolean =>
    (Erlang beamtalk_persistent_term) erase: key
